+# Episode capture acknowledgements no longer wait for search rebuilds
+
+Capture now persists a coalescing `memory-index:pending` obligation before
+acknowledging saved dialogue, while DB-first content, identity tags, Markdown
+parity and independent mirror/cursor boundaries remain intact. The existing
+indexer and standalone watchdog share a version-checked refresh scanner and
+the existing three-arm builder. A per-source database advisory lock serializes
+scanner, straggler and manual rebuild writes; capture takes no such lock.
+Remote failures and missing embedding configuration leave explicit pending
+status. See `docs/episode-capture-indexing.md` for cadence and isolated tests.
+The real recovery source/process was not restarted, replayed or mutated.
+
