new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..429ac28495d013c1452691106c518d6e18da2540
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/episode-capture-indexing.md
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# Episode capture and search refresh
+
+Canonical dialogue and search freshness are separate completion boundaries.
+Capture still saves exact source with its stable identity, appends DB-first to
+the episode, and derives Markdown from the canonical database snapshot. The
+existing independent canonical cursor, mirror outbox and acknowledgement rules
+remain unchanged.
+
+## Durable pending state
+
+`conversation_memories.tags` contains `memory-index:pending` until a complete
+index refresh succeeds. A single marker coalesces multiple appends. The episode
+content UPDATE sets this marker atomically; retry and duplicate paths also
+ensure the obligation exists before reporting completion. Watchdog chat rows
+and personal memories receive the same marker before cursor/state advancement.
+Failure to persist the obligation is an error, not a successful acknowledgement.
+
+The capture acknowledgement does **not** mean search is current. Embedding
+latency or a remote failure cannot hold capture locks, pin saved dialogue, or
+cause source replay just to refresh search.
+
+## Existing indexer owns retry
+
+The existing two-hour `memory-embedding-indexer` scans marked rows as well as
+previously unindexed memories. A standalone watchdog invokes the same pending
+scanner after its capture drains, without awaiting it. There is no extra queue
+table, filesystem queue, or best-effort-only in-memory obligation.
+
+Only IDs are listed up front; large episode contents are read one at a time.
+The worker rebuilds the existing full-content, summary and chunk arms using
+`reembed-memory`. Unchanged hashes skip remote calls; failed/partial work
+retains pending status. Missing embedding configuration or unresolved private
+ownership is a failure, never a successful refresh receipt.
+
+Completion removes only the pending marker, conditional on exact title, summary
+and content equality with the worker's snapshot. A concurrent append retains
+pending for the latest version. Other identity/source tags are preserved.
+
+All conversation-index write paths in the scanner, straggler repair and manual
+rebuild share a transaction-scoped PostgreSQL advisory lock per source ID.
+This works with transaction-pooling endpoints and takes no canonical row lock.
+A busy build leaves the durable obligation pending; it does not block capture.
+
+## Verification
+
+- `npx tsx --test server/services/memory-index-refresh.test.ts`
+- `npx tsx --test server/services/memory-index-refresh-postgres.test.ts`
+- `npx tsx --test server/services/memory-index-rebuild-postgres.test.ts`
+- `npx tsx server/scripts/test-watchdog-chat-capture-attribution.ts`
+- `npx tsx server/scripts/test-watchdog-inner-life.ts`
+
+The PostgreSQL suites require `CI=true`, a verified loopback
+`CI_DATABASE_URL`, and an exactly matching `NEON_SHARED_DATABASE_URL`. The
+real-builder test creates and drops its own database; HTTP embedding responses
+are synthetic within its test process. Neither suite can use the shared live
+episode. CI registration is in `scripts/run-ci-test-steps.mjs`.
+
+No restart, replay or mutation of the real 33-message recovery is part of this
+change. Search may remain pending until the next existing indexer cycle when
+the standalone watchdog is not running.
